WEBVTT

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:01.870
Thank you.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:13.240
me

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:21.800
in a minute.

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:27.980
Are you Vicki McGuire?

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:29.500
Right, yes.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:38.850
won't you come in? I'm Larry Craig's wife. I thought you were dead. I'm sorry to disappoint

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:46.000
you, but I'm very much alive. I understand you're planning to marry my husband. Yes,

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.490
I was planning to. You were gone almost seven years and Larry didn't know where you were.

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:56.200
And according to law, forget the technicalities. It's not that I want him for myself. I most

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:59.750
certainly don't. But he'll never marry you nor anyone else.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:00.720
I'll see to that.

00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:04.250
I wouldn't feel too badly about it, Miss McGuire.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:06.000
I'm doing you a favor.

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:07.190
Good night.

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:36.370
Hello, Athletic Club. Is Larry Craig there?

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:39.860
Club 7-Eleven.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:40.540
Thank you.

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:51.890
Information, will you please give me the number of Club 7-Eleven on Hawthorne Boulevard?

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:53.110
It's...

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:58.830
All your fault, if I'm not sleeping, I live our dreams instead of eating.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:02:59.980
I'm just.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.760
To wreck and it's all your fault

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:11.120
It's all your fault if I'm not playing, having fun, and if I'm staying.

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:14.950
All by myself, well, it's all you're for.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.810
When you said that we were through

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:24.050
I tried to find somebody new, but I found out...

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:24.450
No, no, no.

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:25.720
Wooden booth.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:28.000
Larry Craig, have to see you tomorrow evening.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:28.980
Okay.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:30.360
Oh

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:33.680
But I'm the grandma of my grandkids.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.840
They'll call you grandpa while I'm together.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.060
It's all you're for.

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:45.410
Oh, it's all your fault if I'm not sleeping, I live on three.

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:50.820
Instead of eating, I'm just a wreck and it's all you're for.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:54.600
Hello, Stevie.

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:56.080
Hello, Mr. Craig.

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:57.300
I just had a phone call for you.

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:58.140
Yeah, who is it?

00:03:58.300 --> 00:03:58.880
She wouldn't say.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:03:59.980
She wouldn't tell her to give any message.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.180
Sure enough. Well, give me a double scotch.

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:04.080
Pardon me, Larry. Give me the show.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:06.000
If I was you, I'd sort of sit out the next drink.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:09.460
Listen, Stevie, no lectures, just scotch, huh?

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:10.480
Sure.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:12.880
Sure, why not?

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:14.180
Thank you.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:15.840
I was just laughing at me.

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:19.110
Where's my double scotch?

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:20.250
Oh, it is right in front of you.

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:21.770
Oh, come on, come on.

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:23.070
I gotta have a chaser, Steve.

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:24.790
Come on, stop whippling.

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:26.580
You're the doctor.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:28.200
Nobody loves a peupler, Stevie.

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:30.710
Bye.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:32.680
He's lucky to get back from his trip yet?

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:34.000
Yeah, he got back the other day.

00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:34.640
He did, huh?

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:35.680
He's a great fellow.

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:38.120
He's been a friend of mine for years and years.

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:38.700
When is he?

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:40.340
Well, he was around here a few minutes ago,

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:41.920
but I guess he's out in his office now.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:43.760
Well, I better go check up on him.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:45.060
I don't want to let you get along.

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:53.820
It's all your fault if I'm not playing, having fun, and if I'm staying.

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:55.870
All by myself, well

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:57.860
It's all your fault.

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:05.970
When you said that we were through, I tried to find somebody new.

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:12.230
But I found out it wouldn't do, cause I'd rather be alone than with somebody new.

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:18.670
Oh, it's all your fault when I'm the grandma, my grandkids, they'll call you grandpa.

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:22.590
Well, I'll just tell them it's all your fault.

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:25.300
Thank you.

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:35.510
Hello Lucky!

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:43.570
I didn't hear you knock.

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:45.460
That's funny, I didn't.

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:47.440
This is a private office, you know.

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:48.780
Okay.

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:50.530
I won't let anybody in.

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:04.480
I've seen you like this before.

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:06.240
That's funny.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:07.990
You look different, too.

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:08.800
Oh

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:10.730
Look, Larry, don't you think you're going overboard?

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:12.970
Not that I object to buying a drink.

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:14.980
Well, that stuff isn't exactly a tonic, you know.

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:16.580
A guy doesn't live forever.

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:19.850
What are you celebrating, a long life or an early death?

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:22.430
Don't you worry about me, Lucky.

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:24.060
I can handle my liquor.

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:25.600
Yeah, looks like it.

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:28.500
Just as good as you can handle your women.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:32.140
I don't mix my women with scotch.

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:33.270
Mm.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:34.410
That's fine.

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:36.340
It's got five hands!

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:38.320
1045.

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:40.420
Oh, that's very fast.

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:42.090
Okay, thank you, Vaki.

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:50.620
Oh, I like it.

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:53.960
Now I know what I came in for.

00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:55.760
You have a good trip.

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:57.140
Great trip, great.

00:06:57.580 --> 00:06:58.280
Take it easy, Larry.

00:06:59.080 --> 00:06:59.880
Okay, goodbye.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:00.020
Bye.

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:09.160
You see, you were great tonight.

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:11.560
The best little singer this town's ever had.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:13.300
You look like you're doing pretty good yourself.

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:15.040
I'm gonna go see my girl.

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:17.540
Wonderful. We're going to get married.

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:20.040
Larry, you can't go out like that.

00:07:20.630 --> 00:07:22.590
Why don't you go lie down in my dressing room for a while?

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:25.090
Oh, no, I don't want to lie down. I gotta go see Vicki.

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:28.260
You're in no condition to see anyone.

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:29.100
Come on, Larry.

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:29.600
Yeah.

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:32.340
All right, all right, but just for you.

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:35.260
If it was for anybody else, I wouldn't do it for a minute.

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:38.780
I wouldn't, I'm going to do it, but it's just for you, you understand.

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:40.300
I know it, I know it.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:41.900
Now you lie down, Larry.

00:07:42.470 --> 00:07:44.570
Be a good boy and close your pretty eyes.

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:47.130
You don't want that wonderful girl to see you like this, now do you?

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:49.050
No, no, she might think I'd drink.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:49.840
Yeah

00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:51.240
You

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:53.170
Oh, you're a real pal.

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:54.000
All right.

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:54.790
Amen.

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:26.520
It's about it, let a bitch shout it, don't let anyone kid you, it's a fight.

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:37.620
Oh, he was here early in the evening.

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:39.270
Well, he must have left a couple of hours ago.

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:40.900
Somebody want Larry Craig?

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:41.280
Yeah.

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:43.040
Well, he's asleep in my dressing room.

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:43.860
I'll get him for you.

00:08:44.020 --> 00:08:44.540
Just a minute.

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:45.200
He'll be right here.

00:08:56.520 --> 00:08:56.840
Larry.

00:08:57.530 --> 00:08:58.290
Larry, wake up.

00:08:58.450 --> 00:08:58.590
Huh?

00:08:58.730 --> 00:08:58.910
What?

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:01.210
What are you doing here?

00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:02.720
You want it on the telephone, Larry.

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:04.040
Come on now, pull yourself together.

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:05.710
Yeah, sure.

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:08.140
Ooh, thanks for letting me park.

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:11.280
From now on, I'm going to stick to banana splits.

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:13.000
Where's the phone?

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:13.640
At the bar.

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:14.940
Oh, yeah.

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:17.240
What time is it?

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:18.060
Almost one o'clock.

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:19.300
Yeah, thanks.

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:28.700
Lucky!

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:43.030
Thanks. Hello. Oh, Vicki, darling.

00:09:44.030 --> 00:09:47.130
Oh, Larry, I've been trying to reach you all evening. I must see you.

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:49.380
All right, I'll pick you up in 15 minutes, okay?

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:52.850
All right. Goodbye, Steve.

00:09:53.210 --> 00:09:59.180
I knew she was in town, Vicki. She's been back a couple of weeks.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.060
You should have told me.

00:10:01.180 --> 00:10:02.480
I just have upset you.

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:04.410
I'll have to find out about it sometime.

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:08.860
Look, the day Norma disappeared, we had an appointment with her lawyer.

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:12.200
I'm sure she hasn't had a change of heart as far as I'm concerned.

00:10:13.470 --> 00:10:15.150
I wish I could feel about it as you do.

00:10:15.950 --> 00:10:19.530
But your wife made it quite clear that she had no idea of ever giving you up.

00:10:20.210 --> 00:10:21.710
Norma's just impulsive, that's all.

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:24.710
Her vanity's probably hurt to think I'd want to marry another woman.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:27.160
Where are we going?

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:29.580
Norma's straightening this thing out.

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:31.550
Oh, well, isn't it rather late?

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:34.780
All right, normal keeps rather late hours.

00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:46.130
Larry, would it be all right if I waited here for you?

00:10:46.420 --> 00:10:48.350
Sure, whatever you want, dear. I will be alone.

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:25.220
Larry Craig. Good to meet you, Mr. Craig. My name is Harmon. How do you do? I'd like to see my wife. Me?

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:36.160
What's going on here?

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:38.500
Well, I told you no one was to come in here.

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:39.580
This is Mr. Craig.

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:40.780
He wants to see his wife.

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:42.640
Mrs. Craig is dead.

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:48.010
I'll have to ask you to identify the body.

00:11:57.220 --> 00:11:58.360
Mrs. Craig was murdered.

00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:04.010
What are you doing here?

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:06.750
Why, I'm waiting for Mr. Craig.

00:12:07.310 --> 00:12:08.690
Well, I think you'd better wait inside.

00:12:14.440 --> 00:12:14.960
What's wrong?

00:12:15.140 --> 00:12:16.400
Mrs. Craig has been murdered.

00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:20.200
But I just talked to her a couple of hours ago.

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:21.380
She died kind of sudden.

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:21.850
Come on.

00:12:43.720 --> 00:12:50.370
waiting for him. Oh, Larry, this is Harold. What's your name, miss? Vicki McGuire. Friend of Mrs.

00:12:50.530 --> 00:12:55.230
Craig's? Well, I only met her once, and that was just for a few moments. She's a friend of mine.

00:12:56.980 --> 00:12:59.980
Si. Your wife didn't object to your having...

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:06.320
friends? My wife disappeared almost seven years ago. Prior to that time, we were separated for

00:13:06.320 --> 00:13:12.490
more than a year. Miss McGuire and I are planning to be married when Norma suddenly turned up about

00:13:12.490 --> 00:13:18.950
two weeks ago. That sort of upset your marriage plans? She says she spoke to Mrs. Craig a couple

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:27.420
of hours ago. What did you two talk about? Well... It's all right. Go ahead. We have nothing to hide.

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:29.950
She told me she'd never...

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:36.400
give up, Mr. Craig, and for me to forget about marrying him. What took you guys so long? Higgins

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:40.300
got hooked and it didn't run the game. Where's the body? In there. Come on, I can't wait all night.

00:13:43.890 --> 00:13:48.290
Hi, Captain. Hi, Captain. Why don't people get murdered at a respectable hour? Maybe we could

00:13:48.290 --> 00:13:53.370
pass a law or something. Captain, isn't there someplace else where we could talk? By all

00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:59.970
means. I know this isn't very pleasant. Come on. Be sure.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.440
and get a picture of the mark on her neck.

00:14:02.310 --> 00:14:04.930
Your wife was strangled by a thin wire, Mr. Craig.

00:14:06.590 --> 00:14:07.760
Hold it still.

00:14:10.990 --> 00:14:12.230
Don't let this question bother you.

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:13.920
Where were you two all evening?

00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:16.520
I went to the 7-Eleven club about 10.30.

00:14:16.640 --> 00:14:18.020
I was there until almost 1.

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:19.410
See anyone you knew?

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:20.780
Yes, several people.

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:22.110
I'd like to talk to them.

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:23.380
I have no objections.

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:25.020
How about you, Miss McGuire?

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:26.180
She was at home all evening.

00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:27.220
I talked to her on the telephone.

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:29.540
I think Miss McGuire can answer for herself.

00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:31.950
Well, I was gone for about a half an hour.

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:33.130
I went to a restaurant nearby.

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:34.400
What time was that?

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:37.000
Oh, I should say about 11.30.

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:39.400
Doc, surely you don't suspect either of us.

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:41.060
Just routine.

00:14:44.660 --> 00:14:49.040
Check Miss McGuire's alibi.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.320
She said she went to a restaurant.

00:14:50.440 --> 00:14:50.980
She'll tell you where.

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:52.330
It's okay, take her home.

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:53.220
Yes, Captain.

00:14:53.550 --> 00:14:54.030
Come on, Miss.

00:15:05.440 --> 00:15:06.780
I thought you went home, Mr. Craig.

00:15:07.060 --> 00:15:10.780
I was on my way, Gladys, but this gentleman was curious about where I spent the evening.

00:15:10.980 --> 00:15:11.900
You were here, of course.

00:15:12.240 --> 00:15:13.720
Do you remember what time Mr. Craig came in?

00:15:14.080 --> 00:15:16.600
Not exactly, but I think it was around quarter to eleven.

00:15:17.450 --> 00:15:18.630
Hey, what is this, a quiz?

00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:23.270
My wife has been murdered, Gladys, and I'm number one on the suspect list.

00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:25.080
But you were in the club, Mr. Craig.

00:15:25.340 --> 00:15:26.100
Did you see him leave?

00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:29.640
Why, yes. He took his hat. He checked it with me.

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:31.300
About what time was that?

00:15:31.690 --> 00:15:33.170
It must have been after 12.30.

00:15:33.860 --> 00:15:37.560
I remember because my boyfriend had just called me to tell me he couldn't pick me up.

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:38.530
Thanks, Gladys.

00:15:38.590 --> 00:15:39.230
Who else saw you?

00:15:40.630 --> 00:15:41.990
I had a couple of drinks at the bar.

00:15:53.690 --> 00:15:54.670
Sorry, Larry, but we're closed.

00:15:55.360 --> 00:15:58.720
Steve, you remember my being here earlier this evening, don't you?

00:15:59.060 --> 00:15:59.980
Sure, but I didn't...

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:02.060
you'd remember. You were pretty well lit up.

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:06.080
How long did Mr. Craig stay? Oh, a cup, huh?

00:16:08.040 --> 00:16:10.440
It's all right. Go on, uh, just routine.

00:16:11.220 --> 00:16:12.660
Just know I'm left to have a couple of drinks.

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:14.300
I'd say about 10 or 15 minutes.

00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:17.820
Who else saw you? From here, I went into Lucky

00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:20.040
Brandon's office. I was there for a few minutes.

00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:21.900
Then, on the way out, I bumped into

00:16:21.900 --> 00:16:24.090
Lucille Compton. She's the singer here at the

00:16:24.090 --> 00:16:26.300
club. Uh, she made me take a nap.

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:29.880
What if she's still here? Miss Compton's still here?

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:32.550
I didn't see her go, though she might still be in her dressing room.

00:16:32.740 --> 00:16:33.220
Thanks, dude.

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:35.920
Well, are you satisfied I was here?

00:16:36.440 --> 00:16:38.280
Yes, you have a perfect alibi, Mr. Craig.

00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:40.060
Almost too perfect.

00:16:52.810 --> 00:16:55.030
It's Larry Craig. I have a friend with me. May we come in?

00:16:55.760 --> 00:16:56.360
Come on.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:03.820
Uh, Lucille, this is Captain Brown, Compton.

00:17:03.940 --> 00:17:04.920
Good evening, Miss Compton.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:05.500
How do you do?

00:17:05.800 --> 00:17:07.940
Lucille, you remember my being here earlier this evening?

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:09.540
If you don't mind, I'll ask the question.

00:17:10.460 --> 00:17:11.960
What time did you first see Mr. Craig?

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:13.440
It was after my third number.

00:17:13.520 --> 00:17:14.890
That was about, uh...

00:17:15.190 --> 00:17:15.710
10.55.

00:17:16.190 --> 00:17:18.500
He says he went to sleep here in your dressing room.

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:19.380
Is that right?

00:17:20.070 --> 00:17:20.570
Why, yes.

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:22.600
Say, what's this all about?

00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:23.580
What's happened?

00:17:23.800 --> 00:17:25.840
My wife has been murdered, Lucille.

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:27.110
Oh, no, Larry.

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:29.860
I thought you hadn't heard from her in years.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:30.340
Cheers.

00:17:30.760 --> 00:17:32.320
Well, she came back about two weeks ago.

00:17:33.350 --> 00:17:35.210
The captain here is checking up on me.

00:17:35.940 --> 00:17:37.780
Larry couldn't have had anything to do with it.

00:17:38.090 --> 00:17:40.490
Why, he was asleep on that couch until almost one o'clock.

00:17:42.060 --> 00:17:43.220
Were you with him all that time?

00:17:44.260 --> 00:17:45.640
Of course not. I had to work.

00:17:46.060 --> 00:17:48.860
But I stopped in as often as I could to see if he was all right.

00:17:49.900 --> 00:17:50.620
Good evening, Captain.

00:17:51.020 --> 00:17:53.160
Larry was in no condition to get off that couch.

00:17:54.730 --> 00:17:55.150
Come in.

00:17:59.210 --> 00:17:59.950
Didn't know you were coming.

00:18:00.030 --> 00:18:02.560
Lucille, I just wanted to give you a check.

00:18:02.900 --> 00:18:03.960
I'm glad you came in, Lucky.

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:05.890
You wrong, Captain?

00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:08.960
The Captain just wants to know what time you saw me early this evening.

00:18:09.200 --> 00:18:11.300
Who are you talking about?

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:13.080
I didn't see you this evening.

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:18.480
You must be kidding.

00:18:19.150 --> 00:18:20.390
I was in your office.

00:18:20.890 --> 00:18:21.890
I helped myself to a drink.

00:18:22.090 --> 00:18:24.080
You better lay off that liquor.

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:25.560
Begin to imagine things.

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:28.220
Look, you were at the safe when I came in.

00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:29.580
Surely you must remember.

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:31.570
Look, you better see a psychiatrist.

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:33.110
You weren't in my office.

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:34.560
Not while I was there, anyway.

00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:36.180
This is serious, Lucky.

00:18:36.580 --> 00:18:37.900
Larry's wife has been murdered.

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:41.260
Why, he was right here in this room for a couple of hours anyway.

00:18:42.440 --> 00:18:43.480
So he's got his alibis.

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:44.740
You saw him.

00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:45.680
I didn't.

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:47.360
You're not telling the truth, Lucky, and you know it.

00:18:48.490 --> 00:18:51.090
Come to think of it, I wonder if you might not have a reason for lying.

00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:54.650
When I left here, you were sneaking in the back door.

00:18:55.270 --> 00:18:57.110
I called to you and you pretended you didn't hear me.

00:18:58.020 --> 00:18:58.960
Now I know you were drunk.

00:18:59.120 --> 00:19:00.000
I don't believe there are any...

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:00.660
Any further questions?

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:01.800
Thanks, Lucky.

00:19:07.350 --> 00:19:08.410
Run along now, Mr. Craig.

00:19:08.530 --> 00:19:10.350
If I need you, I'm sure I can find you.

00:19:11.450 --> 00:19:11.950
Thanks, Captain.

00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:13.430
Thank you.

00:19:20.060 --> 00:19:20.480
Captain.

00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:22.130
You don't think he's...

00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:24.160
Possibly could have killed his wife, do you?

00:19:24.920 --> 00:19:26.260
If he was here, he couldn't have.

00:19:27.130 --> 00:19:27.990
Good night, Miss Compton.

00:19:39.590 --> 00:19:40.090
Come in, Captain.

00:19:46.380 --> 00:19:47.140
I didn't see him.

00:19:48.550 --> 00:19:48.770
Thank you.

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:50.200
I believe you're lucky.

00:19:51.530 --> 00:19:52.510
I just want to check a few things.

00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:53.940
Sure.

00:19:55.240 --> 00:19:56.600
You knew Norma Craig, didn't you?

00:19:57.220 --> 00:19:57.500
Yeah.

00:19:57.930 --> 00:19:58.750
friends for a long time.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.820
Wasn't she interested in the 7-Eleven club?

00:20:03.350 --> 00:20:05.570
She loaned me $10,000 when I first opened the club.

00:20:06.170 --> 00:20:07.530
I don't see what that has to do with the murder.

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:10.250
You didn't seem surprised when you heard she was...

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:10.490
dead.

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:13.350
I've got a poker face.

00:20:14.740 --> 00:20:17.920
I wonder why Craig insist he saw you sneak in the rear door of the club.

00:20:18.840 --> 00:20:21.020
He didn't see me sneak in the rear door or any other door.

00:20:21.560 --> 00:20:22.400
for a very good reason.

00:20:23.160 --> 00:20:24.360
I never left the club all evening.

00:20:25.340 --> 00:20:29.300
You're sure you didn't drop over to see Mrs. Craig just to say hello after her long absence?

00:20:30.350 --> 00:20:33.270
Look, Captain, you're wasting your time with me.

00:20:33.810 --> 00:20:34.870
Why don't you try somebody else?

00:20:37.110 --> 00:20:38.820
Well, I guess I'll be running along, Lucky.

00:20:40.670 --> 00:20:41.530
Drop it, I need you.

00:20:42.560 --> 00:20:42.800
Thanks.

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:54.950
Hello?

00:20:55.640 --> 00:20:57.940
Oh, Vicki, darling, I was beginning to worry about you.

00:20:57.940 --> 00:20:58.980
You were so long answering the phone.

00:20:59.410 --> 00:20:59.970
I just got...

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:03.020
The detectives wanted to talk to that girl in the restaurant who waited on me.

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:04.540
We had to go to our boarding house.

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:06.370
Yeah, well, I had quite a session, too.

00:21:06.970 --> 00:21:09.190
Everyone at the club remembered saying me but Lucky Brandon.

00:21:09.980 --> 00:21:11.520
But don't worry, dear, it's going to be all right.

00:21:11.930 --> 00:21:12.110
Hi.

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:14.390
I can't tell you how sorry I am.

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:15.460
dragged you into her.

00:21:16.090 --> 00:21:18.190
Well, it wasn't your fault, Larry. How were you to know?

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:20.750
All right. I'll see you tomorrow.

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:29.000
Thank you.

00:21:36.490 --> 00:21:38.190
Sorry if I startled you, Miss McGuire.

00:21:38.760 --> 00:21:39.720
How did you get in here?

00:21:40.390 --> 00:21:41.490
You left your door unlocked.

00:21:42.440 --> 00:21:43.580
You must have a clear conscience.

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:45.580
What do you want, Captain?

00:21:46.630 --> 00:21:48.170
I just got through talking to Mr. Harmon.

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:51.300
He said the waitress didn't remember what time you were in.

00:21:52.100 --> 00:21:53.640
But she did remember that I was there.

00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:56.460
Why were you so nervous when you were in the restaurant?

00:21:57.540 --> 00:21:59.780
Oh, I don't know. Is Craig coming back?

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:01.280
murder and all those questions.

00:22:02.010 --> 00:22:03.590
You came right back here from the restaurant?

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:04.550
Yes.

00:22:05.500 --> 00:22:06.200
see anyone you knew

00:22:07.670 --> 00:22:08.610
No, I didn't.

00:22:08.820 --> 00:22:11.060
No one call on you? You didn't drop in any other apartment?

00:22:11.770 --> 00:22:14.070
I spent the evening reading and trying to get in touch with Larry.

00:22:15.540 --> 00:22:16.500
Miss McGuire, tell me.

00:22:16.980 --> 00:22:18.840
When do you and Mr. Craig plan on being married?

00:22:19.670 --> 00:22:20.390
Oh, I don't know.

00:22:21.560 --> 00:22:23.180
Certainly not until all this is cleared up.

00:22:24.020 --> 00:22:26.320
If Mrs. Craig hadn't come back, you would be free to marry him.

00:22:26.780 --> 00:22:27.680
in about two months

00:22:28.100 --> 00:22:29.920
Mr. Craig had spoken to a lawyer about it.

00:22:30.500 --> 00:22:31.880
But don't let these questions bother you.

00:22:32.420 --> 00:22:34.520
If I thought for a moment you had anything to do with the murder,

00:22:34.660 --> 00:22:37.640
you would be in jail right now, and that goes for Mr. Craig, too.

00:22:38.280 --> 00:22:38.580
Mm-hmm.

00:22:38.820 --> 00:22:39.740
And why are you here?

00:22:41.030 --> 00:22:42.470
I've got to get all the information I can.

00:22:43.560 --> 00:22:44.080
Just routine.

00:22:45.610 --> 00:22:47.130
Sorry I disturbed you, Mr. Flyer.

00:22:47.590 --> 00:22:47.910
Good night.

00:22:48.420 --> 00:22:48.980
Good night, Kate.

00:22:59.020 --> 00:23:00.000
Sure, Captain Bronson.

00:23:00.060 --> 00:23:00.340
Thanks.

00:23:00.760 --> 00:23:00.960
Yep.

00:23:01.270 --> 00:23:01.830
It's ridiculous.

00:23:02.360 --> 00:23:04.980
He was satisfied with your explanation of where you spent the evening, wasn't he?

00:23:05.560 --> 00:23:06.420
I'm afraid not

00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:09.120
The only person who saw me was the girl in the restaurant.

00:23:09.500 --> 00:23:11.200
She doesn't remember what time she saw me.

00:23:13.400 --> 00:23:15.320
You know, I can't figure him out anyway.

00:23:15.990 --> 00:23:20.990
At least three different people saw me at the 7-Eleven Club and I still don't think he's convinced I spent the evening there.

00:23:22.230 --> 00:23:24.610
I guess he figures my motive is too good to disregard.

00:23:26.010 --> 00:23:27.670
Well as far as the police are concerned

00:23:28.380 --> 00:23:29.920
I wanted Norm out of the way, too.

00:23:31.660 --> 00:23:33.330
Well, nothing we can do about it.

00:23:34.080 --> 00:23:35.540
But in the meantime, I'm hungry.

00:23:35.640 --> 00:23:36.080
How about you?

00:23:36.380 --> 00:23:36.940
I'm stuck.

00:23:49.280 --> 00:23:51.340
Holly, you've got to snap all of it.

00:23:51.650 --> 00:23:52.550
Oh, I'm all right.

00:23:53.040 --> 00:23:53.640
No, you're not.

00:23:54.370 --> 00:23:56.510
Now, look, everything's going to work out fine.

00:23:57.290 --> 00:23:58.030
I hope so.

00:23:58.660 --> 00:23:59.920
I'm afraid this is more serious.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:08.900
than we think hello i'm not intruding oh no no not at all captain no sit down thank you how are

00:24:08.900 --> 00:24:17.520
you mr mcguire fine thank you have some lunch just finished anything new on the case not a thing the

00:24:18.700 --> 00:24:26.580
murder was pretty clever you left no fingerprints and absolutely no clues mr craig why did you and

00:24:26.580 --> 00:24:29.960
your wife separate i don't know just didn't get

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:34.460
long, I guess. Maybe it was my fault. It wasn't because she helped him start the 7-Eleven club,

00:24:34.580 --> 00:24:40.940
was it? No. Oh, although I knew about that. You see, I never questioned my wife about what she did

00:24:40.940 --> 00:24:47.810
with her money, Captain. It was hers. She inherited it from her mother. I didn't sleep

00:24:47.810 --> 00:24:56.480
very well last night. I'm thinking about something you said. You're sure you saw Brandon slip into

00:24:56.480 --> 00:24:59.510
the club? Yes, I'm quite sure.

00:25:00.700 --> 00:25:03.860
Was he interested in your wife, that is, personally?

00:25:04.750 --> 00:25:08.380
I don't know, although I always had the feeling Norman was quite fond of him.

00:25:09.240 --> 00:25:11.720
And you didn't leave the club, not even for a little while?

00:25:12.490 --> 00:25:14.930
No, Captain, not even for a little while.

00:25:16.960 --> 00:25:19.980
I'm going to have to do something pretty soon.

00:25:20.660 --> 00:25:22.460
DA is getting very impatient.

00:25:23.400 --> 00:25:28.080
Look here, Captain Brock, I've established where I was the night of the murder.

00:25:29.080 --> 00:25:29.900
You don't believe it.

00:25:31.120 --> 00:25:33.700
Miss McGuire is the last person in the world you should suspect.

00:25:34.300 --> 00:25:36.670
And yet you pop up in her apartment, I suppose,

00:25:36.670 --> 00:25:39.190
hoping that she'll say something to incriminate herself.

00:25:40.170 --> 00:25:42.470
Now, you're not following us around because you're lonesome.

00:25:43.090 --> 00:25:44.690
If you think we're guilty, why don't you arrest us?

00:25:45.670 --> 00:25:47.010
You're jumping at conclusions.

00:25:48.160 --> 00:25:48.900
Merely routine.

00:25:50.440 --> 00:25:51.780
Well, I don't like your routine.

00:25:52.600 --> 00:25:54.000
Well, I must be running along.

00:25:55.080 --> 00:25:56.120
Goodbye, Miss McGuire.

00:25:56.670 --> 00:25:57.130
Bye, Kevin.

00:26:00.350 --> 00:26:03.330
Sure would like to know why Brandon wouldn't alibi for you.

00:26:03.450 --> 00:26:05.860
Good day.

00:26:11.760 --> 00:26:14.100
Larry, I wonder why he did deny that he saw you.

00:26:14.540 --> 00:26:15.280
I wish I knew.

00:26:16.200 --> 00:26:18.900
Captain Brown evidently thinks he had something to do with the murder,

00:26:19.000 --> 00:26:20.790
or he wouldn't have brought up his name.

00:26:21.590 --> 00:26:23.830
Maybe when I saw Lucky sneaking in the back of the club,

00:26:23.850 --> 00:26:25.580
he was coming back from Norma's.

00:26:25.920 --> 00:26:28.600
He wouldn't recognize me because he wanted an alibi for himself.

00:26:29.480 --> 00:26:29.980
He couldn't.

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:36.600
bear watching. Larry, I could do it. Do what? Watch him. Well, I could get a job in the

00:26:36.600 --> 00:26:40.350
club. He doesn't know me. I thought you didn't like nightclubs. Well, what difference does

00:26:40.350 --> 00:26:44.520
that make? Maybe I could find out something that even the police couldn't. Vicki, you're

00:26:44.520 --> 00:26:49.260
not serious. Don't you realize that if Brandon is the murderer and he finds you snooping

00:26:49.260 --> 00:26:52.680
around the club, your life wouldn't be worth a plug nickel. And don't you realize the

00:26:52.680 --> 00:26:59.640
spot we're in? Well, I've got to do it. Oh. Uh, is Mr. Brandon here? He won't be here

00:26:59.640 --> 00:26:59.980
for a couple

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:04.300
of hours. Oh, pardon me. Are you the girl

00:27:04.300 --> 00:27:06.040
who photographs the guests here? Yes.

00:27:06.380 --> 00:27:08.470
Could I see you for a moment? Sure. Come to the

00:27:08.470 --> 00:27:14.110
dark room. I upload some plates. What's on your mind,

00:27:14.210 --> 00:27:16.060
kid? How would you like a vacation?

00:27:17.400 --> 00:27:19.090
Who wouldn't? Look,

00:27:19.530 --> 00:27:21.450
here's $50. I want your job

00:27:21.450 --> 00:27:24.140
for a couple of days. Say, I do. You've got

00:27:24.140 --> 00:27:26.100
to help me out. There's a guy here I'm just

00:27:26.100 --> 00:27:28.160
crazy about, and he doesn't even know that I exist.

00:27:28.750 --> 00:27:29.850
All I want to do is get acquainted.

00:27:30.440 --> 00:27:31.620
Say, who is this lucky Romeo?

00:27:33.000 --> 00:27:33.640
The bartender.

00:27:35.080 --> 00:27:35.360
Steve?

00:27:35.640 --> 00:27:38.020
I don't know what there is about the guy that he just sends me.

00:27:38.620 --> 00:27:39.780
Now I've heard everything.

00:27:40.000 --> 00:27:40.520
Will you do it?

00:27:42.210 --> 00:27:43.230
Do you want to work one of these cameras?

00:27:43.550 --> 00:27:44.450
Of course, that's easy.

00:27:44.950 --> 00:27:45.430
What do you think?

00:27:47.610 --> 00:27:50.180
I'll do it, but believe me, you're making a bad deal.

00:27:50.980 --> 00:27:51.260
Thanks.

00:27:54.510 --> 00:27:55.350
Hiya, Margie.

00:27:56.900 --> 00:27:57.900
Let me look at you, Steve.

00:27:59.090 --> 00:27:59.970
Hey, what's going on?

00:28:00.460 --> 00:28:02.370
Maybe I'm crazy.

00:28:02.830 --> 00:28:04.990
Well, I ain't gonna argue that part with you, Margie.

00:28:05.740 --> 00:28:08.940
Steve, a gal just came in here and gave me 50 bucks to take my place.

00:28:09.000 --> 00:28:10.180
Just so she could be near you.

00:28:10.620 --> 00:28:12.280
Huh? What's the matter with her?

00:28:13.140 --> 00:28:14.040
That's what I'd like to know.

00:28:15.360 --> 00:28:16.260
Irresistible, that's all.

00:28:17.020 --> 00:28:18.610
Well, so long, Casanova.

00:28:56.970 --> 00:28:59.960
Make a nice souvenir if you visit the Club 7-Eleven.

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:02.930
Are you new here?

00:29:03.330 --> 00:29:04.790
Oh, no, I've been here a long time.

00:29:05.640 --> 00:29:06.340
How would you like it?

00:29:07.240 --> 00:29:07.900
On a profile?

00:29:09.270 --> 00:29:10.330
Straight on, if you don't like it.

00:29:13.640 --> 00:29:14.760
Ah, look at me and smile.

00:29:16.780 --> 00:29:17.960
How are you tonight, Mr. Brandon?

00:29:19.010 --> 00:29:19.910
Hello, Pep, how are you?

00:29:20.350 --> 00:29:21.690
Will you have a drink with us, Mr. Brandon?

00:29:22.600 --> 00:29:22.880
Thanks.

00:29:23.420 --> 00:29:24.760
I can dish it out, but I can't take it.

00:29:24.900 --> 00:29:26.020
Well, some other time, Lucky.

00:29:26.220 --> 00:29:26.520
You bet.

00:29:31.880 --> 00:29:32.910
You could destroy that picture.

00:29:34.780 --> 00:29:35.680
Yes, Mr. Brant.

00:29:41.140 --> 00:29:53.300
My mouth opened.

00:29:53.620 --> 00:29:54.640
Is that something new?

00:29:54.990 --> 00:29:56.410
I'll have it for you in about a half hour.

00:30:12.540 --> 00:30:14.320
Brave man, eating in your own place.

00:30:15.240 --> 00:30:15.820
I'm used to it.

00:30:16.700 --> 00:30:17.020
Join me?

00:30:17.580 --> 00:30:18.140
Oh, thank you.

00:30:18.700 --> 00:30:21.180
Been watching the papers, and I see you haven't cracked that Craig case yet.

00:30:21.320 --> 00:30:22.800
Just be slipping.

00:30:24.300 --> 00:30:25.620
How did you and Norma Craig stand?

00:30:26.380 --> 00:30:26.940
Meaning what?

00:30:27.700 --> 00:30:29.120
She owned a bit of this place, didn't she?

00:30:30.090 --> 00:30:31.250
Fade off a long time ago.

00:30:32.380 --> 00:30:33.900
You're a hard man to discourage, Captain.

00:30:34.120 --> 00:30:37.280
To keep this up, you're going to have me believing that I'm under suspicion.

00:30:38.060 --> 00:30:39.960
Everyone is until this case is cleared up.

00:30:41.640 --> 00:30:43.070
Well, this will be running along.

00:30:44.250 --> 00:30:45.230
I'll be seeing you, Lucky.

00:30:46.390 --> 00:30:47.010
I don't doubt it.

00:31:06.650 --> 00:31:08.110
Well, I got one. I hope it's all right.

00:31:08.520 --> 00:31:09.440
You'll soon find out.

00:31:11.920 --> 00:31:12.420
Anything wrong?

00:31:12.920 --> 00:31:13.940
Why, no, Mr. Brandon.

00:31:14.770 --> 00:31:16.720
Oh, Bill, uh, go in and get me a couple of cigars here.

00:31:16.860 --> 00:31:17.200
Yes, sir.

00:31:18.450 --> 00:31:19.130
What happened to Marge?

00:31:19.890 --> 00:31:20.730
She was taken ill.

00:31:20.930 --> 00:31:22.830
She asked me if I could help her out for a few days.

00:31:23.810 --> 00:31:24.390
Did she tell me?

00:31:24.810 --> 00:31:26.710
Well, I'm sure I don't know what happened so suddenly.

00:31:27.730 --> 00:31:29.590
Maybe I'd better call her up and see if there's anything I can do.

00:31:29.790 --> 00:31:29.970
Oh, no.

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:36.480
Oh, no. She didn't go to her home. She's staying with a sick aunt, and she mustn't be disturbed.

00:31:46.510 --> 00:31:47.590
You learn to work one of these things.

00:31:48.820 --> 00:31:52.430
I've been around the camera a lot. I've been a photographic model for years.

00:31:54.080 --> 00:31:55.600
I'd like to see some of the pictures you've made.

00:31:56.200 --> 00:31:57.320
Well, a few of them will be developed.

00:31:57.340 --> 00:31:58.440
The iris is completely closed.

00:31:59.140 --> 00:31:59.320
Oh.

00:32:00.510 --> 00:32:02.330
Oh, well, it must have just happened, Mr. Brandon.

00:32:05.210 --> 00:32:06.210
Here are your cigars, Mr. Brandon.

00:32:06.820 --> 00:32:07.440
Oh, thanks, sir.

00:32:13.230 --> 00:32:15.110
Hey, your boss seems like a nice guy.

00:32:15.410 --> 00:32:16.370
Yeah, but don't let it get you.

00:32:16.410 --> 00:32:17.930
He's got a lot of women crazy about him.

00:32:18.770 --> 00:32:19.690
Any one in particular?

00:32:20.820 --> 00:32:23.020
Oh, I understand this Norma Craig who was murdered.

00:32:23.490 --> 00:32:24.510
She used to run around with him.

00:32:25.450 --> 00:32:26.860
Uh, did you ever see her?

00:32:27.200 --> 00:32:28.260
Yeah, a couple of nights ago.

00:32:28.300 --> 00:32:29.140
She came into the club.

00:32:29.430 --> 00:32:29.970
The boy was listening to...

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:32.080
Neil Compton saw. She thought she had the inside

00:32:32.080 --> 00:32:34.440
track. Then this Craig woman shows up

00:32:34.440 --> 00:32:35.920
after being gone seven years.

00:32:36.810 --> 00:32:38.910
Lucille ain't getting no place either. She's only

00:32:38.910 --> 00:32:41.930
kidding herself. Gosh, I'm glad I'm not

00:32:41.930 --> 00:32:53.890
pretty. I can't get away with it, Lucky. After

00:32:53.890 --> 00:32:55.850
all I've done for you, the least you could do is show me

00:32:55.850 --> 00:32:58.780
a little consideration. For your own good, I suggest

00:32:58.780 --> 00:32:59.980
you don't have an affair with my business.

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:02.410
You said, yeah? You have nothing to worry about.

00:33:02.730 --> 00:33:04.630
Well, I'll give you something to worry about.

00:33:05.250 --> 00:33:08.220
I know where you went Tuesday night. Norma Craig!

00:33:09.350 --> 00:33:10.510
Talk to you about that later.

00:33:33.130 --> 00:33:34.950
Is there anything I can do, Miss Compton?

00:33:35.170 --> 00:33:36.830
No. Leave me alone.

00:33:37.840 --> 00:33:40.760
I couldn't help overhearing your conversation with Mr. Brandon.

00:33:40.940 --> 00:33:41.780
Oh, forget it, kid.

00:33:43.030 --> 00:33:44.630
I've heard a lot about Norma Craig.

00:33:45.480 --> 00:33:46.600
Did you know her very well?

00:33:46.740 --> 00:33:48.190
Yes. Too well.

00:33:49.110 --> 00:33:50.370
Believe me, that woman had it coming.

00:33:51.620 --> 00:33:54.320
From what I understand, she had a way of stirring up trouble.

00:33:54.460 --> 00:33:56.030
Yeah. See where it got her?

00:33:57.570 --> 00:33:59.970
Say, did you ever hear of her...

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:07.080
husband, Larry Craig? Sure. Everybody's interested in the Craig murder. What about Mr. Craig?

00:34:08.200 --> 00:34:18.350
Well, he and Mrs. Craig were... Yes? You're on, Miss Compton. Talk to you some other time, kid.

00:34:36.360 --> 00:34:37.880
Surprised seeing you here, Miss McGuire.

00:34:38.810 --> 00:34:43.270
Just a hunch, Captain, but I think you'll find the answer of who killed Norma Craig right here in this club.

00:34:44.450 --> 00:34:47.550
Lucille loves Brannon, and she accused him of being in Norma's house the night of the murder.

00:34:54.020 --> 00:34:56.740
If we hadn't been interrupted, I know Lucille would have told me plenty.

00:34:57.100 --> 00:34:58.100
What were they arguing about?

00:34:58.720 --> 00:34:59.960
Well, I got in on the tail end of...

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:02.440
But she accused Brannon of being at Norma's the night of the murder.

00:35:02.930 --> 00:35:03.570
That's interesting.

00:35:03.900 --> 00:35:04.600
Did he deny it?

00:35:05.120 --> 00:35:07.420
No, he just cut her short and told her he'd talk to her later.

00:35:08.020 --> 00:35:09.000
Did you tell Captain Brown that?

00:35:09.160 --> 00:35:09.440
Mm-hmm.

00:35:10.440 --> 00:35:13.080
He seemed very interested in something the boy in the developing room told me.

00:35:13.940 --> 00:35:16.080
Norma came to see Brannon at the club a couple of days ago.

00:35:17.740 --> 00:35:19.840
Say, do you know Lucille very well?

00:35:20.400 --> 00:35:20.600
Why?

00:35:20.820 --> 00:35:21.580
No, not well.

00:35:21.720 --> 00:35:22.260
Why do you ask?

00:35:23.230 --> 00:35:24.430
She asked me if I knew you.

00:35:25.450 --> 00:35:28.290
She was about to say something concerning you when she was called out.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:33.890
Vicki, I wish you'd forget this business of playing detective.

00:35:34.600 --> 00:35:36.120
Now, you've given the police a couple of leads.

00:35:36.320 --> 00:35:37.400
Why don't you let them handle it?

00:35:38.210 --> 00:35:41.270
Look, Larry, I've started something, and I've got to see it through.

00:35:41.900 --> 00:35:43.180
I worry about you, Vicki.

00:35:43.460 --> 00:35:44.400
You shouldn't.

00:35:44.760 --> 00:35:46.260
Captain Brown stick's pretty close.

00:35:48.040 --> 00:35:50.220
Your mother raised a very stubborn little girl, Vicki.

00:35:51.310 --> 00:35:52.710
I think I'll marry you just the same.

00:35:54.330 --> 00:35:58.360
You know, Larry, lucky Brandon isn't at all what I expected him to be.

00:35:58.750 --> 00:35:59.190
He isn't?

00:36:00.020 --> 00:36:01.640
No, in the first place, he's much younger.

00:36:02.420 --> 00:36:03.420
It sort of frightens me.

00:36:05.210 --> 00:36:06.970
There's still something fascinating about the man.

00:36:07.800 --> 00:36:09.400
Maybe it's his voice or his eyes.

00:36:09.500 --> 00:36:10.600
Hey, wait a minute.

00:36:11.220 --> 00:36:12.480
You're not falling for him, are you?

00:36:12.980 --> 00:36:14.780
You know I don't fall that easily.

00:36:15.740 --> 00:36:16.220
I know that.

00:36:18.870 --> 00:36:19.050
off.

00:36:38.630 --> 00:36:39.050
Hello, Larry.

00:36:40.360 --> 00:36:40.820
Well...

00:36:41.000 --> 00:36:42.100
Surprised you recognize me.

00:36:43.210 --> 00:36:43.970
What are you so worried about?

00:36:44.360 --> 00:36:45.280
Didn't kill Norma, did you?

00:36:46.120 --> 00:36:46.800
You know I didn't.

00:36:48.260 --> 00:36:49.340
Too bad Norma showed up.

00:36:50.340 --> 00:36:51.360
You were all set to get married.

00:36:51.980 --> 00:36:52.080
You know?

00:36:54.020 --> 00:36:54.580
Who told you that?

00:36:55.820 --> 00:36:56.320
Don't carry a pigeon.

00:36:57.610 --> 00:36:58.130
Tell me it.

00:36:58.540 --> 00:37:00.000
Who is a lucky girl you're so crazy about?

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:01.560
Why don't you ask the pigeon?

00:37:16.720 --> 00:37:16.960
Thank you.

00:38:02.490 --> 00:38:02.752
Thank you.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:30.880
Thank you.

00:38:39.560 --> 00:38:39.780
be

00:38:40.700 --> 00:38:42.140
Give Stevie a little kiss.

00:38:42.360 --> 00:38:43.780
Oh, now listen, what are you doing in here?

00:38:43.840 --> 00:38:45.280
Get back to the bar, you'll lose your job.

00:38:45.400 --> 00:38:47.240
You talk like we're married already, honey.

00:38:47.600 --> 00:38:49.020
Come on, give baby a kiss.

00:38:49.220 --> 00:38:49.880
Oh, please, Steve.

00:38:50.200 --> 00:38:51.400
I don't understand you women.

00:38:51.500 --> 00:38:53.240
One woman's act like you're crazy about a guy,

00:38:53.400 --> 00:38:55.000
and the next woman's act like you're just crazy.

00:38:55.240 --> 00:38:56.800
Give Steve your little, little kiss.

00:38:58.150 --> 00:38:58.770
What's going on here?

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:00.580
We were just talking.

00:39:01.430 --> 00:39:02.690
You mind if I enter into the conversation?

00:39:03.350 --> 00:39:04.010
Get back to work.

00:39:04.680 --> 00:39:05.100
Yes, sir.

00:39:07.450 --> 00:39:07.990
How did this happen?

00:39:08.470 --> 00:39:11.110
Well, I don't know. I think Steve had the wrong idea of me.

00:39:11.770 --> 00:39:12.810
I'll have him fry it in the morning.

00:39:12.970 --> 00:39:13.670
Oh, please don't.

00:39:13.730 --> 00:39:15.410
I'm sure he won't try anything like that again.

00:39:16.440 --> 00:39:17.200
Oh, just a minute, please.

00:39:18.140 --> 00:39:18.820
Yes, Mr. Brandon.

00:39:19.290 --> 00:39:19.970
How did you get in here?

00:39:20.820 --> 00:39:23.480
Oh, your door was open. I was looking for some plates for my camera.

00:39:34.160 --> 00:39:34.660
There you are, miss.

00:39:35.050 --> 00:39:35.810
Thank you, Mr. Brandon.

00:39:36.780 --> 00:39:38.180
Sorry it went such a hurry this afternoon.

00:39:38.500 --> 00:39:39.420
We might have had lunch together.

00:39:40.900 --> 00:39:41.900
with Larry Craig, weren't you?

00:39:42.440 --> 00:39:42.760
Bye.

00:39:42.920 --> 00:39:43.800
Yes, I was.

00:39:44.360 --> 00:39:46.520
I'd be more careful in choosing my friends if I were you.

00:39:48.200 --> 00:39:49.200
Let be all, Mr. Brandon.

00:39:50.860 --> 00:39:51.080
Yeah.

00:39:51.910 --> 00:39:52.310
time being.

00:40:30.350 --> 00:40:32.760
Hello there, this is Vicki.

00:40:45.320 --> 00:40:47.660
Thank you.

00:41:01.370 --> 00:41:02.350
Thank you.

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:30.980
Thank you.

00:43:47.020 --> 00:43:48.640
How long will it be, dear?

00:44:00.220 --> 00:44:00.760
Dad

00:44:02.070 --> 00:44:03.530
Close to me, darling.

00:44:07.100 --> 00:44:07.840
To the moon.

00:45:02.330 --> 00:45:03.310
Thank you.

00:45:14.390 --> 00:45:15.030
I'm gonna kill you, Lucky.

00:45:19.190 --> 00:45:20.230
That gun down, let's see.

00:45:21.240 --> 00:45:21.680
what you're doing.

00:45:22.170 --> 00:45:23.150
Oh, yes, I do.

00:45:23.900 --> 00:45:25.760
You're not going to toss me over and get away with it.

00:45:27.420 --> 00:45:28.400
Thank you.

00:45:37.690 --> 00:45:43.600
Was anybody hurt?

00:45:44.880 --> 00:45:45.520
No, it's all right.

00:45:45.620 --> 00:45:46.560
The gun went off accidently.

00:45:46.640 --> 00:45:47.240
I didn't know it was loaded.

00:45:50.040 --> 00:45:50.960
Close that door, will you miss?

00:45:56.110 --> 00:45:57.530
Is there anything I can do, Mr. Brandon?

00:45:58.140 --> 00:45:59.660
I wonder if you mind taking Miss Compton home.

00:46:00.470 --> 00:46:01.530
Pull yourself together, let's see.

00:46:01.910 --> 00:46:02.630
We love you all right.

00:46:15.670 --> 00:46:16.590
How do you feel alright?

00:46:17.430 --> 00:46:18.130
I think so.

00:46:18.580 --> 00:46:20.180
I'll go change my clothes and be back in a minute.

00:47:03.770 --> 00:47:04.030
Hello?

00:47:05.080 --> 00:47:07.440
Oh, hello, Vicki. What happened before you hung up on me?

00:47:07.830 --> 00:47:08.930
Things are happening fast.

00:47:09.080 --> 00:47:11.260
Lucille tried to shoot Brandon and I'm going to take her home.

00:47:12.280 --> 00:47:14.340
This is my chance to get her to talk, but keep your fingers cut.

00:47:15.410 --> 00:47:17.210
She might even tell me something about you.

00:47:18.070 --> 00:47:19.110
All right, I'll speak to you later.

00:47:19.410 --> 00:47:19.910
Goodbye, Mary.

00:47:20.340 --> 00:47:20.760
Goodbye, dear.

00:47:24.630 --> 00:47:25.210
Oh, are you ready?

00:47:25.780 --> 00:47:27.940
I don't think it's necessary for you to see me home.

00:47:28.440 --> 00:47:30.000
Oh, I wouldn't think of letting you go.

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:30.440
alone.

00:47:36.010 --> 00:47:36.830
Just a minute, please.

00:48:17.020 --> 00:48:17.520
down that alley.

00:48:18.040 --> 00:48:18.480
I don't know.

00:48:18.550 --> 00:48:18.990
Compton.

00:48:19.320 --> 00:48:20.340
Are you afraid you're being followed?

00:48:20.790 --> 00:48:21.090
No.

00:48:21.680 --> 00:48:22.600
I'm just a little nervous.

00:48:34.630 --> 00:48:35.730
Thanks for seeing me home.

00:48:41.420 --> 00:48:43.060
If you'd like, I'd be glad to spend the night.

00:48:43.260 --> 00:48:44.840
Oh, I'm sure I'll be all right now.

00:48:45.130 --> 00:48:46.610
I really don't think you should be alone.

00:48:46.730 --> 00:48:47.650
No, thanks. Just the same.

00:48:48.490 --> 00:48:50.410
I feel pretty safe now that I'm in my apartment.

00:48:51.110 --> 00:48:51.530
Good night.

00:48:52.010 --> 00:48:52.570
Thanks again.

00:48:53.510 --> 00:48:53.870
Good night.

00:49:30.600 --> 00:49:31.940
What did you tell her?

00:49:33.500 --> 00:49:34.280
What are you doing here?

00:49:36.800 --> 00:49:39.370
What did you tell her?

00:49:39.990 --> 00:49:41.150
What did I tell who?

00:49:41.870 --> 00:49:42.170
Vicki.

00:49:43.660 --> 00:49:45.140
I didn't tell her anything.

00:49:50.650 --> 00:49:52.010
Don't look at me like that.

00:49:52.900 --> 00:49:53.840
Thought she could run away.

00:49:54.040 --> 00:49:57.230
No, I did everything you asked.

00:49:57.800 --> 00:49:58.800
I alibized for you.

00:49:59.490 --> 00:49:59.910
Oh, Larry.

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:00.040
Bye.

00:50:01.300 --> 00:50:01.880
Hilarious!

00:50:02.680 --> 00:50:03.360
You can't!

00:50:05.880 --> 00:50:06.700
Keep my mouth shut.

00:50:07.220 --> 00:50:07.400
I-

00:50:08.380 --> 00:50:09.180
I'll keep your secret!

00:50:09.740 --> 00:50:10.840
I want her dead.

00:50:30.060 --> 00:50:30.400
Bye-bye.

00:50:31.080 --> 00:50:32.200
Oh, Captain Brown.

00:50:32.940 --> 00:50:33.180
Oh!

00:50:34.220 --> 00:50:37.720
I found that in Brandon's desk. He paid Norma Craig $10,000 for something.

00:50:38.360 --> 00:50:39.720
This may be very valuable.

00:50:39.920 --> 00:50:41.080
It's dated on the night of a murder.

00:50:42.760 --> 00:50:45.000
See, maybe that's where Brandon went when Larry saw him.

00:50:45.160 --> 00:50:46.140
Thank you.

00:50:46.180 --> 00:50:48.400
I was surprised when I saw you come home with Miss Compton.

00:50:48.620 --> 00:50:49.620
I didn't know you were friends.

00:50:49.860 --> 00:50:51.040
Well, Brandon asked me to.

00:50:51.300 --> 00:50:53.600
They had some sort of a squabble and she tried to shoot him.

00:50:54.280 --> 00:50:56.640
I thought maybe I could get her to talk, but she wouldn't let me stay.

00:50:57.380 --> 00:50:59.980
Come on, Miss McGuire. I have a few questions to ask her.

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:00.420
myself.

00:51:22.170 --> 00:51:23.430
We've gone out without our thing, huh?

00:51:25.340 --> 00:51:26.560
Hey, what's going on here?

00:51:26.970 --> 00:51:28.170
You'll wake up all my tenants!

00:51:28.500 --> 00:51:29.940
Are you the manager of this apartment house?

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:30.720
You bet I am.

00:51:30.950 --> 00:51:32.390
Get out of here, I'll call an officer.

00:51:33.260 --> 00:51:34.260
I am an officer.

00:51:35.340 --> 00:51:36.440
We'd like to get in that apartment.

00:51:37.290 --> 00:51:38.550
Have you got a search warrant?

00:51:38.690 --> 00:51:39.810
Please, let us in the apartment.

00:51:39.950 --> 00:51:40.870
Miss Thompson may need it.

00:51:41.540 --> 00:51:42.740
Oh well, alright.

00:52:18.040 --> 00:52:18.860
Just a few minutes.

00:52:26.000 --> 00:52:27.780
I knew by a wire, just like Norma Craig.

00:52:28.570 --> 00:52:29.970
If I hadn't left her, maybe this wouldn't have...

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:38.440
happened you know i always thought miss compton was implicated in this somehow well she evidently

00:52:38.440 --> 00:52:43.940
thought someone wanted to kill her say she tried to take a shot at brandon yes but he took the

00:52:43.940 --> 00:52:59.770
gun away from her i wonder if he could have followed her home a man come down the fire escape

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:01.340
Tried to follow him, but he gave me the slip.

00:53:01.660 --> 00:53:03.540
Phone headquarters. Get the boys over here right away.

00:53:03.980 --> 00:53:05.000
We've had another murder.

00:53:05.910 --> 00:53:06.230
Okay.

00:53:07.270 --> 00:53:08.590
Take you home as soon as they get here.

00:53:20.250 --> 00:53:21.130
Good night, Miss McGuire.

00:53:21.330 --> 00:53:21.990
Good night, Captain.

00:53:34.830 --> 00:53:34.970
Mary!

00:53:35.650 --> 00:53:36.650
I was worried about you.

00:53:37.690 --> 00:53:38.590
Something terrible's happened.

00:53:39.050 --> 00:53:40.110
Lucille Compton's been murdered.

00:53:40.390 --> 00:53:41.290
I just left her apartment.

00:53:42.520 --> 00:53:42.840
Lucille, murdered?

00:53:43.560 --> 00:53:43.980
Who killed her?

00:53:44.360 --> 00:53:46.000
If we knew that, we'd know who killed Norma.

00:53:46.580 --> 00:53:47.920
She was strangled the same way.

00:53:49.310 --> 00:53:50.430
It's like a nightmare, isn't it?

00:53:52.080 --> 00:53:53.140
Come on, let's take a little drive.

00:53:53.340 --> 00:53:54.660
You won't be able to sleep after this.

00:53:54.660 --> 00:53:55.300
I know I won't.

00:54:05.240 --> 00:54:09.440
with her. Did you catch even a glimpse of the murderer? No, he must have been waiting on the fire

00:54:09.440 --> 00:54:15.780
escape for me to leave. How do you know it was a man? One of the policemen saw him, but he got away.

00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:00.760
What's the matter?

00:55:01.600 --> 00:55:02.760
What did Lucille tell you?

00:55:03.730 --> 00:55:04.250
Why, nothing.

00:55:04.390 --> 00:55:05.410
She didn't have a chance to.

00:55:05.750 --> 00:55:06.870
You're keeping something from me.

00:55:07.290 --> 00:55:08.210
What did Lucille tell you?

00:55:09.270 --> 00:55:10.930
Why should I keep anything from you?

00:55:11.460 --> 00:55:12.560
I'm sure I don't know.

00:55:14.200 --> 00:55:15.800
Larry, you're acting awfully strange.

00:55:16.300 --> 00:55:16.620
Am I?

00:55:18.630 --> 00:55:22.260
I guess I'm just a little upset, that's all.

00:55:22.500 --> 00:55:23.380
I understand.

00:55:23.800 --> 00:55:24.540
Let's forget him.

00:55:32.330 --> 00:55:38.960
Hey, you. Is that your car over there?

00:55:39.760 --> 00:55:40.080
Yes.

00:55:40.800 --> 00:55:41.660
I see your driver's license.

00:55:41.780 --> 00:55:52.980
What are you doing around here?

00:55:54.380 --> 00:55:55.640
Taking a walk, getting some air.

00:55:56.450 --> 00:55:57.410
Well, you'd better move along.

00:55:57.980 --> 00:55:59.580
There's been a lot of robberies around here.

00:56:01.020 --> 00:56:01.280
Alright?

00:56:01.560 --> 00:56:01.820
Thanks.

00:56:30.380 --> 00:56:31.940
Thanks for the ride, Larry. Good night.

00:56:32.080 --> 00:56:33.000
Aren't you going to ask me out?

00:56:33.640 --> 00:56:34.720
Well, it's rather late, Larry.

00:56:35.270 --> 00:56:36.030
Just for a little while.

00:56:36.670 --> 00:56:37.710
I'm afraid not.

00:56:38.150 --> 00:56:39.410
I'll see you tomorrow. Good night.

00:57:08.540 --> 00:57:10.960
Would you please send a cab to 4468 Hillhurst?

00:57:11.260 --> 00:57:12.360
As soon as possible, please.

00:57:30.760 --> 00:57:31.780
7-Eleven Club, please.

00:58:30.000 --> 00:58:30.980
Thank you.

